                <pb facs="0533" n="499" xml:id="pg499"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-09-09"><hi rendition="#italic">September 9, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received Sept. 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 752.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of Department’s No. 752, of the 25th ultimo, relative to the tobacco case of
                    Messrs. Sartorius &amp; Co., and to inform you that in compliance with your
                    instructions I have submitted to the Spanish Government the additional evidence
                    inclosed in the Department’s No. 714, of June 25 last, and asked for a
                    reexamination and favorable decision of the case in the light of said additional
                    evidence.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
